{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And the land which I gave to Abraham and to Isaac, to you I will give it</b> — just as I gave it to them, so I will give it to you. This hints at the oath, for to them it was given with an oath, so that sin would not nullify it, whereas to him it was given at the outset without an oath. And this is what is said everywhere (Exodus 33:1 and elsewhere): \"which I swore to Abraham, to Isaac, and to Jacob.\" Alternatively, the repetition of the prophecy to him constitutes an oath, as I have already explained."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:39:32.067166901Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}